macOS InputMethodKit client for IBus
====================================

`ibus-macos` is an experimental Input Method Kit (IMK) client that
forwards key events from macOS applications to `ibus-daemon` through
`IBusInputContext`.

Build
-----

The client is enabled automatically when configuring on Darwin:

    meson setup build
    meson compile -C build

On other hosts, pass `-Dmacos-im=enabled` (requires an Objective-C
compiler and the macOS SDK). Typical macOS flags when GTK/X11
dependencies are not installed:

    meson setup build \
      -Dgtk3=false -Dgtk4=false -Dui=false \
      -Dappindicator=false -Dlibnotify=false \
      -Demoji-dict=false -Dunicode-dict=false \
      -Dgtk-doc=false -Dsystemd-services=disabled \
      -Dsetup=false

Install as an input method
--------------------------

The IMK executable is installed as an application bundle:

    $prefix/libexec/IBus.app

Copy or symlink it into the Input Methods folder, then enable IBus in
System Settings → Keyboard → Input Sources:

    cp -R $prefix/libexec/IBus.app ~/Library/Input\ Methods/
    # log out and back in, then add "IBus" as an input source

`ibus-daemon` must be running (for example from a Homebrew prefix)
before the input method can create an input context.

Architecture
------------

* `IBusIMController` subclasses `IMKInputController` and maps `NSEvent`
  key events to IBus keyvals / modifier masks.
* Preedit is shown as marked text in the client application.
* Lookup tables and auxiliary text are rendered by `ibus-ui-macos`
  (`ui/macospanel`), which implements `IBusPanelService`.
